    "body": "A block of mass $M_A$ = \\textbf{19.0 kg} and a specific heat $C_A$ has an initial temperature of $T_A$. It is brought into thermal contact with a second block of mass $M_B$ = \\textbf{23.0 kg} and specific heat $C_B$ at temperature $T_B$. When the two blocks are brought in contact then come to equilibrium temperature $T_F$. \n\n\\textbf{Block A's} temperature has increased by $\\triangle T_A$ = \\textbf{7.0 K} while Block B's temperature has decreased by $\\triangle T_B$ = \\textbf{19.0 K}.\n\nWhat is the value of the ratio of their specific heats $\\frac{C_B}{C_A}$? \\textbf{Select the closest answer.}",
